IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dpa-types`
IMPORT `dpa-rules`

-- Death Penalty Abolition Act 1973 (Cth) — the encoder's tests.

§ `Tests`

cth MEANS `Offence` OF `a law of the Commonwealth`, TRUE
terr MEANS `Offence` OF `a law of a Territory`, TRUE
imp MEANS `Offence` OF `an Imperial Act within the Parliament's powers`, TRUE
state MEANS `Offence` OF `a law of a State`, TRUE
other MEANS `Offence` OF `some other law`, TRUE
cthNoDeath MEANS `Offence` OF `a law of the Commonwealth`, FALSE
stateNoDeath MEANS `Offence` OF `a law of a State`, FALSE

#ASSERT `death may be imposed for` cth EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `death may be imposed for` terr EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `death may be imposed for` imp EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `death may be imposed for` state EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `death may be imposed for` other EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `death may be imposed for` cthNoDeath EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `the penalty in place of death for` cth EQUALS JUST `imprisonment for life`
#ASSERT `the penalty in place of death for` terr EQUALS JUST `imprisonment for life`
#ASSERT `the penalty in place of death for` imp EQUALS JUST `imprisonment for life`
-- Changed after the independent pass: the Act sets no replacement for a
-- State law (F1).
#ASSERT `the penalty in place of death for` state EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the penalty in place of death for` other EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the penalty in place of death for` cthNoDeath EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the penalty in place of death for` stateNoDeath EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`the death penalty position for` cth)'s `the Act applies`
#ASSERT (`the death penalty position for` state)'s `the Act applies`
#ASSERT NOT ((`the death penalty position for` other)'s `the Act applies`)
#ASSERT (`the death penalty position for` other)'s `death may be imposed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the death penalty position for` terr)'s `the penalty in place of death` EQUALS JUST `imprisonment for life`
